T*
(SAFETY DATA SHEET \(SDS\) - GHS / OSHA HAZCOM STANDARD) Tj
T*
(Document Code: SDS_80-15-9 | Revision: R1) Tj
T*
(Chemical Name: Cumene Hydroperoxide \(alpha,alpha-Dimethylbenzyl Hydroperoxide, 80-82 wt% in Cumene\)) Tj
T*
(CAS Number: 80-15-9 | UN Number: UN 3109 \(Organic Peroxide Type F, Liquid\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. HAZARD IDENTIFICATION & REACTIVE THERMAL HAZARDS) Tj
T*
(- GHS Classifications:) Tj
T*
(  * Organic Peroxide Type F \(H242: Heating may cause a fire or explosion\)) Tj
T*
(  * Acute Toxicity Oral/Dermal Category 3, Inhalation Category 2) Tj
T*
(  * Skin Corrosion Category 1B \(Causes severe skin burns and eye damage\)) Tj
T*
(- Self-Accelerating Decomposition Temperature \(SADT\): 75.0 degC \(for prolonged unstirred storage\); maximum continuous process film temperature in Unit 2300 V-2301 is strictly limited to 105.0 degC.) Tj
T*
(- Exothermic Decomposition Energy: -1580 kJ/kg CHP \(liberates non-condensable methane, oxygen, acetone, and acetophenone vapors\).) Tj
T*
